---
layout: compress
swcache: true
---
{%- comment -%}
  Local override of Chirpy's search index.

  Polyglot filters `site.posts` to the active language and builds a separate
  copy of this file per language (default at the site root, others under
  `/<lang>/`). However, the post URLs here live inside a JSON string, not an
  `href="..."` attribute, so polyglot does NOT add the language prefix to them.
  Without help, the English index would link results back to the Chinese
  (default) URLs. We add the active language prefix explicitly below.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign url_prefix = '' -%}
{%- if site.active_lang and site.active_lang != site.default_lang -%}
  {%- assign url_prefix = '/' | append: site.active_lang -%}
{%- endif -%}
[
  {% for post in site.posts %}
  {
    "title": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
    "url": {{ post.url | relative_url | prepend: url_prefix | jsonify }},
    "categories": {{ post.categories | join: ', ' | jsonify }},
    "tags": {{ post.tags | join: ', ' | jsonify }},
    "date": {{ post.date | jsonify }},
    {% capture content -%}{% include post-summary.html full_text=true %}{%- endcapture -%}
    "content": {{ content | jsonify }}
  }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
]
